27:["$","h2","h2-3",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"IAM: The Thing That Will Actually Break Your Architecture"}]
28:["$","p","p-10",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"The most common cloud security failure is not \"someone hacked in\" — it's \"the developer gave the Lambda function admin permissions because it was easier.\" IAM is boring and tedious and absolutely critical."}]
29:["$","p","p-11",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Principles I follow:"}]
2a:["$","ol","ol-0",{"className":"space-y-1 mb-4 ml-4 list-decimal","children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Least privilege always"}],": every Lambda, ECS task, and EC2 instance gets an IAM role with only the specific permissions it needs"]}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"No long-lived access keys"}],": use IAM roles and instance profiles, never hardcoded keys"]}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Enable CloudTrail"}],": API call logging is free and invaluable for debugging (\"why did this fail at 3am?\")"]}]]}],"\n"]}]
2b:["$","div","pre-0,code-0",{"className":"my-4 cyber-glass p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"font-code text-xs text-cyber-green whitespace-pre","children":"{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [{\n    \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n    \"Action\": [\"s3:GetObject\", \"s3:PutObject\"],\n    \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-specific-bucket/*\"\n  }]\n}\n"}]}]
2c:["$","p","p-12",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":["Not ",["$","code","code-0",{"className":"font-code text-xs bg-cyber-blue/10 text-cyber-blue px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded","children":"s3:*"}],". Not ",["$","code","code-1",{"className":"font-code text-xs bg-cyber-blue/10 text-cyber-blue px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded","children":"*"}],". Specific actions, specific resources."]}]
2d:["$","h2","h2-4",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"RDS vs. DynamoDB vs. Aurora Serverless"}]
2e:["$","p","p-13",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Use RDS (PostgreSQL)"}]," when: you have relational data with complex queries, your team knows SQL, and you need ACID transactions. This is the right default for most applications."]}]
2f:["$","p","p-14",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Use DynamoDB"}]," when: you need single-digit millisecond reads at any scale, you know your access patterns in advance, and you don't need ad-hoc queries. DynamoDB is excellent but requires upfront schema design that's completely different from relational modeling."]}]
30:["$","p","p-15",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Use Aurora Serverless v2"}]," when: you have an RDS workload but traffic is highly variable and you want to save on idle costs. It scales down to near-zero and back up in seconds."]}]
31:["$","h2","h2-5",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"Cost Control: The Architecture Skill Nobody Talks About"}]
32:["$","p","p-16",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"AWS can be devastatingly expensive when you're not careful. Things that surprise people:"}]
33:["$","ul","ul-2",{"className":"space-y-1 mb-4 ml-4","children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Data transfer out"}]," is not free. Egress from EC2/RDS/ELB to the internet costs money. Keep your services in the same AZ when possible."]}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"NAT Gateway"}]," charges per GB transferred. Use it only for services that truly need outbound internet access."]}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"CloudWatch Logs"}]," storage adds up. Set retention policies on every log group."]}]]}],"\n"]}]
34:["$","p","p-17",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":["I set up ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"AWS Budgets"}]," with email alerts at 80% and 100% of budget on every account I manage. It takes 5 minutes and has saved me from several \"I left a GPU instance running\" situations."]}]
35:["$","h2","h2-6",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"The Architecture Philosophy"}]
36:["$","p","p-18",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"The best AWS architecture is the one that's simple enough for your team to operate at 2am when something breaks. Always ask: \"what happens when this component fails?\" If the answer is \"we're down,\" either add redundancy or accept the risk explicitly. Don't assume it won't happen."}]
